            "beats": [
              {
                "text": "“Quiet so far,” Nera says, glancing toward the notice board. “Mostly waiting for someone to ask about the work. I try not to hover when people read the notices. Nobody likes someone looking over their shoulder.”\n\nShe gives a small, rueful smile. “Not that I'm particularly good at waiting.”",
                "requiresEffects": []
              },
              {
                "text": "With your attention still on her, she leaves it at that for a moment rather than turning the conversation toward business.\n\n“It's kind of you to ask, Ari. How has yours been?”",
                "requiresEffects": []
              }
            ],
            "visualDescription": {
              "text": "Morning light falls across the village notice board. Nera faces Ari in the square, with the shallow millrace and its narrow plank crossing nearby.",
              "requiresEffects": []
            }
          }
        }
